title Chess Server Design - Matthew Rahm
actor Client
participant Server
participant Handler
participant Service
participant DataAccess
database Database

// Proposed interactions for Phase 3; database operations describe the storage contract.
group #navy Register #white
Client -> Server: POST /user\n{username, password, email}
Server -> Handler: registerHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: deserialize JSON into RegisterRequest
break malformed JSON
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: register(RegisterRequest)
break missing username, password, or email
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getUser(username)
DataAccess -> Database: find user by username
Database --> DataAccess: UserData or null
DataAccess --> Service: UserData or null
break UserData is not null
Service --> Handler: throw AlreadyTakenException
Handler --> Server: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
Server --> Client: 403 {"message":"Error: already taken"}
end
Service -> Service: hashPassword(password)
Service -> DataAccess: createUser(UserData(username, passwordHash, email))
DataAccess -> Database: store UserData
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service -> Service: generateToken() using UUID.randomUUID()
Service -> DataAccess: createAuth(AuthData(authToken, username))
DataAccess -> Database: store AuthData
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: RegisterResult(username, authToken)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON
Handler --> Server: 200 {username, authToken}
Server --> Client: 200 {username, authToken}
end

// Alternative termination of Register if any data access operation fails.
group #gray Register storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During any database operation above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end

group #orange Login #white
Client -> Server: POST /session\n{username, password}
Server -> Handler: loginHandler(context)
Handler -> Handler: deserialize JSON into LoginRequest
break malformed JSON
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Handler -> Service: login(LoginRequest)
break missing username or password
Service --> Handler: throw BadRequestException
Handler --> Server: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
Server --> Client: 400 {"message":"Error: bad request"}
end
Service -> DataAccess: getUser(username)
DataAccess -> Database: find user by username
Database --> DataAccess: UserData or null
DataAccess --> Service: UserData or null
break UserData is null
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> Service: passwordMatches(password, user.password)
break password does not match the stored hash
Service --> Handler: throw UnauthorizedException
Handler --> Server: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
Server --> Client: 401 {"message":"Error: unauthorized"}
end
Service -> Service: generateToken() using UUID.randomUUID()
Service -> DataAccess: createAuth(AuthData(authToken, username))
DataAccess -> Database: store new AuthData; preserve other sessions
Database --> DataAccess: stored
DataAccess --> Service: return
Service --> Handler: LoginResult(username, authToken)
Handler -> Handler: serialize result to JSON
Handler --> Server: 200 {username, authToken}
Server --> Client: 200 {username, authToken}
end

// Alternative termination of Login if any data access operation fails.
group #gray Login storage error #white
note over Service,Database: During any database operation above; stop the normal flow.
Database --> DataAccess: storage failure
DataAccess --> Service: throw DataAccessException
Service --> Handler: propagate DataAccessException
Handler --> Server: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
Server --> Client: 500 {"message":"Error: internal server error"}
end
